Benefits and Challenges
Benefits:
Reduces system errors and improves reliability.
Improves system speed and performance.
Saves development and maintenance time.
Provides better security and user experience.
Makes future updates easier.
Challenges:
Modernization may require additional cost.
Old data may be difficult to migrate.
Developers need training to use AI tools.
AI-generated code may contain errors and requires human review.
System updates may temporarily affect college activities.
Conclusion
Software maintenance, software reengineering, and AI-assisted software engineering play an important role in modernizing the existing Student Management System.
Software maintenance helps fix errors and improve features. Software reengineering improves the structure and performance of the old system. AI tools help developers detect bugs and automate software testing.
By combining these techniques, the college can develop a faster, more reliable, secure, and user-friendly Student Management System.
